#! ia 1.0

@phase orient
  meaning
    says "Establish the objective, context and constraints before selecting work."
    answers "Does the work still lack a clear objective, the context it rests on or its limits?"
  data
    order 0

@phase plan
  meaning
    says "Derive a bounded approach and the evidence that will establish its result."
    answers "Does the work have a settled goal but still need an approach and the evidence that will prove it?"
  data
    order 1

@phase act
  meaning
    says "Perform the authorized work and observe its actual effects."
    answers "Does the work have an authorized approach and now need doing, with its real effects watched?"
  data
    order 2

@phase learn
  meaning
    says "Compare the outcome with the intent and retain attributable knowledge."
    answers "Does the work have an outcome to hold against the intent, and knowledge worth keeping?"
  data
    order 3

